  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best (config_043, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in a multiprofile setup. All four aggregation×fusion combinations with this encoder pair have been tested, so the multiprofile design space is exhausted. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the multiprofile aggregation step is truly necessary or whether singleprofile with the same strong encoders and weighted fusion can approach this performance at lower cost. config_038 (singleprofile, scvi_n200, vit_l, weighted) directly tests this: it retains the two best-performing encoders and the best fusion strategy while removing the aggregation step. If it performs near 0.725, it offers a significantly cheaper alternative (~2-3 GPU hours vs ~3.6-4.8); if it falls well short, it confirms multiprofile aggregation is essential. This is the best use of the penultimate experiment because it either finds a cost-effective near-equivalent or definitively closes the design question, leaving the final experiment free to either confirm or explore a marginal variant. Expected relative cost: low (~2-3 GPU hours, roughly half the cost of the multiprofile transformer configs)."
}

